THIRD-PARTY LICENSES
====================

The PdfCraft embed build is a WebAssembly module compiled from PdfCraft's own source, the
open-source Rust crates listed here and the Rust standard library (its notices are at the end).
PdfCraft's own licences are in LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE and NOTICE in this bundle; the licence
texts of the fonts, icons, CMaps and colour profiles compiled into the module are in licenses/.

How to read the list:

- Each section gives one licence text and the crates it applies to. The text is the crate's own
  licence file, so the copyright holders are the ones that file names. Where the crate's package
  has no usable licence file, the file comes from the crate's source repository at the commit the
  package was published from.
- A crate whose files keep the holder lines apart from the licence terms (the REUSE layout) has
  two sections: the holder lines, and the terms.
- Some licence files name no holder. For those, the authors declared in the crate's metadata are
  shown in parentheses beside the crate; they may not be complete.
- The Apache License 2.0 text names no holder by design. A crate that carries only that standard
  text is shown with its metadata authors in the same way.
- A crate offered under several licences ("MIT OR Apache-2.0") is listed under the first of them
  that PdfCraft accepts. A crate that also contains code under another licence is listed under
  each.
- The crates named pdfcraft-* are PdfCraft's own, under the licence in LICENSE-MIT.
- The list was generated by cargo-about from Cargo.lock for the crates compiled into the module
  for wasm32-unknown-unknown (no build scripts, no tests). Procedural-macro crates that only run
  at build time are included as well.

